{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Prevention remediation for incident 1c0d (CI/test lane)\n\nPost-mortem: `9097-2741-6462-424c`. This is the detection guard that would have caught the incident before prod: a contract/regression test asserting that any provider transient failure degrades to a retryable disposition, never a hard INDETERMINATE.\n\n### Problem it guards\n\nA throttled primary (429/`WAIT_AND_RETRY`) that fails over to an uncredentialed fallback surfaced as `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` -> INDETERMINATE. The 1c0d fix (change 2404) added a held-out oracle for the specific keyless-`TypeError` case, but there is no broad contract test pinning the class invariant.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test drives a real `build_fallback_model` chain using mocked providers and zero live Bedrock where the primary raises retryable transients (throttle 429, timeout, and 5xx) and the terminal fallback arm raises a non-retryable credential/config error; the classified disposition is retryable (exit-11 class), never `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`/INDETERMINATE.\n- [ ] A vocabulary/closure assertion proves a `FallbackExceptionGroup` is classified by its most-recoverable leg (retryable wins), while an all-non-retryable group maps to `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`, never `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`.\n- [ ] The regression oracle is mutation-sensitive to the pre-2404 class by reverting the two relevant seams locally/behind the sandbox: fallback-leg retention and fallback-group most-recoverable classification.\n- [ ] The test runs in the normal `make test` matrix, with no network and no CI-provider-specific trigger.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py tests/unit/test_llm_failure_classifier.py` and the pre-push `make verify` gate from the ticket worktree.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is test-only and adds no intended behavior. It complements epic 3405-c0b7's exhaustive `exception->code` contract test (same discipline, different taxonomy: this pins the `ResolutionClass` disposition, 3405 pins the workflow error-code vocabulary)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788754191006940001,"uuid":"74c5861b-ee1d-4dc3-a3a6-d7c34badda98"}